  "question": {
    "text": "The area bounded by the parabolas $y=4 x^2, y=\\frac{x^2}{9}$ and the line $y=2$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "cx2ru",
      "text": "$\\frac{5 \\sqrt{2}}{3}$ sq. units",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "fWaD4",
      "text": "$\\frac{10 \\sqrt{2}}{3}$ sq. units",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "tzo6K",
      "text": "$\\frac{15 \\sqrt{2}}{3}$ sq. units",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "wL4Fn",
      "text": "$\\frac{20 \\sqrt{2}}{3}$ sq. units",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints: $y=4 x^2$\n$$\ny=\\frac{x^2}{4}\n$$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& A=\\int_{\\mathrm{r}}^2\\left[\\frac{\\sqrt{y}}{2}-3 \\sqrt{y}\\right] d y=\\left(\\frac{1}{2}-3\\right) \\int_0^2 \\sqrt{y} d y \\\\\n& =\\left(\\frac{-\\sqrt{\\mathrm{y}}}{2}\\right) \\frac{5}{3}\\left(\\mathrm{y}^{3 / 2}\\right)_0^2=-\\frac{5}{3}(2 \\sqrt{2}-0) \\\\\n& =\\left|-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\right|=\\frac{10 \\sqrt{2}}{3} \\text {, Area of bounded figure }=2 \\mathrm{~A}=\\frac{20 \\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\\n&\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
